<BaseLayout title="Alternator" description="LS alternator excite wire, Holley 197-400 pigtail, and Holley flex/alternator input setup for Genesis Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>Alternator</h1>
  <p>
    You need to run a 12V trigger wire for the alternator to charge your battery. It must have a resistor on it — it <strong>cannot</strong> be a straight wire, so buy the right part.
    You can wire it into a Holley ECU or tap into one of the driver's-side fuse box wires.
  </p>

  <h2>Simplest Option: GM 4-Pin Pigtail</h2>
  <p>
    Holley's 197-400 pigtail plugs into the GM 4-pin oval alternator connector and has a 560 ohm, 1/2 watt resistor inline.
    Run its lead to a switched 12V source that's live in the ignition <em>run</em> position. You can route it through a charge light if you want a warning when the alternator stops charging.
  </p>

  <h2>Holley Setup</h2>
  <p>
    I bought a Sloppy Mechanics harness that plugs into the Holley power tap and wired it into the Holley white/red input harness, <strong>J1-A3</strong> (the flex fuel input).
    Holley configuration is shown below.
  </p>
  <div class="note"><p><strong>Edit:</strong> set this input as <strong>digital frequency</strong>.</p></div>
